question.stem_en:
A developer is building a LangChain agent that needs tools from two MCP servers. Server A is a legacy server (pre-`2026-07-28` protocol) and Server B supports the modern protocol. She writes the following code:

```python
from langchain.mcp import MCPAdapter

CONFIG = {
    "mcpServers": {
        "server_a": {"url": "http://legacy.example.com/mcp"},
        "server_b": {"url": "http://modern.example.com/mcp"},
    }
}

async with MCPAdapter(CONFIG) as adapter:
    tools = await adapter.list_tools()
```

What is the consequence of passing both servers as a single `MCPConfig` fleet instead of using a `ClientGroup` with separate clients?

